An update's picture painted into the last one's region (Kosmos webkit.md
Fast, step 1b; testing.md 18.856). The web process made a region the size
of the dirty bounds for every update - for a scrolled frame the view's, as
the scrollbar runs down its edge: 3.3 MB, 0.7 ms on the M700. Only the
dirty rectangles are painted and only they are taken in, so once the UI
process has answered the update before (DidUpdate, which display() waits
for), its picture serves for the next of the same size. Never in
updateGeometry, whose update is sent without waiting for an answer.

diff -ru a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaCoordinatedGraphics.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaCoordinatedGraphics.cpp
